			Let \(\sigma\coloneqq-[\sigma_{\sDRS}]_-=\min\set{\sigma_{\sDRS},0}\) and \(L\geq L_{\sDRS}\) be such that \(L+\sigma>0\); the value of such an \(L\) will be fixed later.
			Then, \(\sigma\leq0\) and \(\sDRS\) is \(L\)-smooth and \(\sigma\)-hypoconvex.
			We may thus choose \(\rho(u,u^+)\) as in \cref{thm:hypo:rho1} with these values of \(L\) and \(\sigma\).
